[{"id":"VRCE-6-56-1","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":1,"english":"Seeing Kumbhakarņa slain by the high-souled Rāghava, the Räkşasas conveyed the tidings to the lord of the Raksasas-Ravana; (and addressed him, saying)","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056001","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4e536c4f35c71f1050d9c7a3a112e938128f61877c8f0fcbd7692b8c2a6685c1","compact":"9768491e81501988d005665283178d98c6a7b4aa9e9e24cb06fd875f558d7b8d","nasal":"1900aca7efae692bfe7963f5a66bf66c88d4c4c477cddc5bf14b73081bba8e4a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-2","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":2,"english":"Hearing the mighty Kumbhakarņa slain in battle, Ravana burning in grief, swooned away and dropped to the earth.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.86,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056002","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d3bedab484b5966f8319e324d221be47323ae7c3ab33aca87e31c93a75240dd0","compact":"8da2939e913f3962cba6beb859340ff239b43fc4e9de6564041a60ab50fcb220","nasal":"c99264cdc2706c86e35a0714c70cb26d76b1d1b178ee44375d655c3d000df6ea"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-3","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":3,"english":"Hearing their uncle slain, Trisiras* and Atikāya-destroyers of gods and men, began to weep, oppressed with sorrow. *Three-headed.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056003","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"13a638a10427b27694234dbcc1b0a6b825bce9e1fe8ac132bec2a4fb0aae50f8","compact":"ba9f76e64cb111ecb58d7913165be0e64ad8557c77a62b5db7b02f9e36c935f2","nasal":"b2f9e314acc42c6e489ad8e0857c329df8be6bfe99f8a8abf8d49604ae1ab78f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-4","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":4,"english":"Mahodara' and Mahāpārśvahearing of their uncle slain by Rāma of untiring deeds, were overcome with grief. 1. Huge-bellied. 2. Mighty flanked.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.806,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056004","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cbbadbec615c60a1f46d1c48a59caf3f058c4cf5278a7f369e392658d6af5fb8","compact":"49c265441189bd12eb3da661e5e2f81d43ed8f10fcbdfcc5d88b0cc85af769af","nasal":"a608f90a74838f1528d8d5b32b7ce4dfb987cd12256980af9395396d9c9a30a7"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-5","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":5,"english":"Then regaining his senses with extreme exertion, that foremost of Rākṣasas, distressed in consequence of the destruction of Kumbhakarna, mourned with his senses overwhelmed, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.619,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056005","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a6d68ce4120f2d71e35139c4c50c8cc4dee1717fa5ca4a9f3b7c734c607f0935","compact":"b0678484daae49e2962948771553c54c195cc4f611d0463396618b7470f5c7e2","nasal":"e3de5d667a47d7ac16934948d995e844b712c1d3714019286c8f6ee41a2e83f6"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-6","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":6,"english":"O hero! O humbler of the pride of the foe! O mighty Kumbhakarna! Leaving me, you through stiny, have gone to the abode of Yama. O exceedingly powerful one, leaving me (alone) whither did you wend, without extracting my dart as well as that of your friends?","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.615,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-7","DUTT-6-68-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056006","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8a832ec1c4ba88f40d25a787bd5ead968db2caa458e954c4a8a0d9f3e04afe81","compact":"cc6a13fbd75e4c825f8a650285dfe37099ed225be4742b2918aa9c9a83f05e55","nasal":"3ced965fe5e7a946905027453b191bfb74f1b54fa0b3679258b1b98fe04fb201"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-7","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":7,"english":"Now really I am not, inasmuch as my right arm has dropped. Backed by this one, I would not fear celestials and Asuras.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.968,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056007","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"56977ed2c2ef732cfffaef2f62b4df852e60d95366900e271a35370577a2e5e4","compact":"ae228b02faf2503ae9d2f66107d43006b60a8c5da448160bcc897deadc9d8cbd","nasal":"ae228b02faf2503ae9d2f66107d43006b60a8c5da448160bcc897deadc9d8cbd"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-8","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":8,"english":"How today forsooth has such a hero-crusher of the hauteur of gods and Dänavas—resembling the fire arisen at the hour of universal wreck, been slain in fight by Raghava?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056008","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"eae0339aab149ff8c7b387f27b56e1dbc22f02f0b94596279a945fc8e43ecfa7","compact":"d74356d63c5715a9b2dc537022a80021861370e6adcc0eaf71213317f9940513","nasal":"d74356d63c5715a9b2dc537022a80021861370e6adcc0eaf71213317f9940513"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-9","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":9,"english":"He who could not be harmed by the concussion of the thunder-bolt itself-how can he, smitten with Rāma's arrows, sleep soundly on the earth?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056009","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d30f0ed0d2efb80c2647e82cfde75565dffe15f84c3553f6f63dc73304294a88","compact":"be1c028b6bbb3bdce224e1da334b46c612622bd2059b9bf8c887c6143a114e69","nasal":"be1c028b6bbb3bdce224e1da334b46c612622bd2059b9bf8c887c6143a114e69"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-10","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":10,"english":"These gods stationed in the sky along with the saints, beholding you slain the battle, are shouting in glee.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056010","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4f712386686c9eb0cd6eb73c9304fd15ad360041f3d5b7f6993425c7269d9b4a","compact":"c963eb09987ad482d87e389d7c3ab20ca0d8b5977f387d031faeac74417ea8d8","nasal":"ed1c9c0a74849b835f98af212a9040060051018df447423f2f425dc568fadeca"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-11","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":11,"english":"Surely today the monkeys overjoyed, finding occasion, well scale all the gateways and fortifications of Lankā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ce3211702358520de18dc0f6f4d9becc0506646010b0c446a9504812dfcfde1e","compact":"18fa4c6feec0b92f66f461dcfda4ae7c7b969c496de025af06dd9d6f4b29901e","nasal":"7dd21380e6283bfdc8b603df2b7a30e090121d34f3a4acc70b575bbb58c0036f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":12,"english":"I have nothing to do with empire. And what shall I do with Sītā? And deprived of Kumbhakarma, I do not even wish to live.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.818,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d82aec4c997354fb9f814261a88ea806521b283c03fb566c6c2270dd9c3f3635","compact":"f5a1f114566538a58e13337b2c03e4642018d7d5e996728257a6f40860f9844c","nasal":"8d0be21aa341a8d7b8f80ea0339a22454419303e9d8433271632e7273883c37a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":13,"english":"If I do not slay in encounter that slayer of my brother-Rāghava, certainly death is even that which is good for me, otherwise, this life is useless.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.967,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9b3ac717d06fd88385b3c2f5b68aa0c69ceae68701934b706848497ae428e8d2","compact":"7e628c8fe91a9232222b64ef2aca03c677f16e10efa7600634fc0820fa70c51c","nasal":"d75ef9bb0c91c21abce32040aef294546a80753a7d192b2a4ecbdaca8e04423f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":14,"english":"This very day will I repair to that place where my younger brother is. Forsaking my brother, I forsooth dare not live for a moment.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"78db0ea84c7ec4efc117f287c308d33f0681759d58b090f628187d3c3a16caab","compact":"737859812c58b61c13c8a930116a1fe578e09851efa695e34ae676457fe9ac9e","nasal":"737859812c58b61c13c8a930116a1fe578e09851efa695e34ae676457fe9ac9e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":15,"english":"For the gods shall laugh on seeing me, who had formerly wronged them. But, how, O Kumbhakarņa, you having been slain, shall I conquer Indra?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f0fc73d7a55b1ad5d2151bc7d7b7995d8931c8fdbe1a6325c17eb4deed34a755","compact":"e7121b307c159aab80f4f2efa872115598cbeb0749286f4b7171db4445dcdc1d","nasal":"a439426e2ae9bda5af34afeaa2b95f7a3f9b92746947a517fe8ec7355446b074"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":16,"english":"Now the beneficial words of Vibhīşaņa have been verified. And as through blindness I did not accept the advice of that high-souled one, Kumbhakarņa and of Prahasta, this disaster arisen, shame me sore.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e2f4de2cf5e4a57363b769dc73a5e7c41aaa7e42e6a8989553b44490df661a24","compact":"34704e9012fe547839c6ee166342ff906f6e9e7b783c3d7fe42ff5888746fec2","nasal":"34704e9012fe547839c6ee166342ff906f6e9e7b783c3d7fe42ff5888746fec2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":17,"english":"Now the beneficial words of Vibhīşaņa have been verified. And as through blindness I did not accept the advice of that high-souled one, Kumbhakarņa and of Prahasta, this disaster arisen, shame me sore.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.607,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a68af2df2d8b241ebb2b2b6e64ef88896364e1a321ca99f7e4ee5cf3e24d1e50","compact":"427b17f3445f914233a4241eb7724edf9c6bcaf74383720c7c76f18eb72fc268","nasal":"46454741409ca116e3f9e0e0f9090de82bb896cb100e9210b77676201a6f0ad4"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":18,"english":"As I had disgraced the virtuous and graceful Vibhīşaņa, this peril producing grief, has been the consequence of my conduct.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.887,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ea2fd1a359e3efde29e11b7d8631e56e0461865ff2567d70a8f6e59f8e97ac63","compact":"3999746e2f7e5198e084f8f2b749948bffca04186f80283c0b4d4cb5de06868e","nasal":"3999746e2f7e5198e084f8f2b749948bffca04186f80283c0b4d4cb5de06868e"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-56-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":56,"verse":19,"english":"Having thus piteously and long lamented Kumbhakarna, the Ten-necked one, with his inmost soul overwhelmed with sorrow, and sore distressed in consequence of grief, fell down, knowing his brother—the enemy of Indra-slain in battle.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.707,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-68-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6056019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1a0698a8507168bda36245d602d67de17c552066d618e6bb915397a185a64834","compact":"463ba087d066d228d85f9670c4e28f6c218b3d1f151f956dd2ddfcd6a49ba078","nasal":"c8e6e35e6db0a93645dae58be9d4b954af324ec548ad923bade0d6a362010d9c"}}]
